. Smaller centers"This basic settlement patterna dominant center surrounded by a cluster of smaller settlements and lower densities of population at greater distances from the center"<br>Secondary centres (e.g. Huitzo, Tomaltepec, El Mogote)El Mogote was 25ha and these sites had their own public buildings (such as the 3m high adobe structure at Tomaltepec)<br>3. Satellite settlements of the smaller centers"Clusters of settlements were established around these new centers, which may have been the head towns of small, spatially discrete polities that had variable degrees of autonomy from San Jose Mogote (Blanton et al., 1999, pp. 43-44)."<br>Villages (e.g. Fábrica San José, San Sebastián Abasolo, Tierras Largas).95-3ha'}], {'usage.total_tokens': 1021, 'usage.prompt_tokens': 914})
